  "name": "minixiangqi",
  "description": "Minixiangqi, xiangqi on a 7x7 board without a river, devised in 1973 by Shigenobu Kusumoto. Each side has two chariots, two cannons, two horses, a general and five soldiers; there are no advisors or elephants. Soldiers step forward or sideways from the start, the horse is blocked by a piece beside it, the cannon takes by jumping one piece, and the general stays in its 3x3 palace and may never face the other across an open file. A player with no legal move loses. One departure: perpetual check and chasing are counted as an ordinary repetition draw rather than forbidden.",
